<title>BELGIUM: EU clears 345 mln shillings in aid to BMW.</title>
<headline>EU clears 345 mln shillings in aid to BMW.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had cleared a proposal by the Austrian authorities to grant 345 million shillings to German carmaker BMW to help develop an investment project in Steyr.</p>
<p>It said the aid package would allow BMW to extend production capacity for petrol and diesel engines used in its assembly plant in Spartanburg, in the United States, and in Rover cars.</p>
<p>The project, which is financed by national and regional grants, started in 1996 and will be completed in the year 2000.</p>
<p>The Commission took into consideration, when clearing the aid, that the project presented technological advances and would contribute to reduce car gas emission and to preserve jobs.</p>
</text>
